        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. What do we know of the US's 15-point peace plan sent to Iran? Middle East Issued on: 25/03/2026 - 12:28 Modified: 25/03/2026 - 12:29 Donald Trump says he has a 15-point plan that has been offered to Iran to bring an end to the war. But details remain vague and Trump's claims of progress in talks have been dismissed by Tehran. The US is hoping that talks hosted by Pakistan will be able to facilitate a settlement. But Washington is still keeping its military options open, with US media reporting that at least 3,000 airborne troops would be deployed to the region in the coming days. Inside the Palestinian camp in Beirut where residents are staying put, for now 25/03/2026 Middle East In Lebanon, some schools choose to stay open despite the war 25/03/2026 Middle East US ramps up military presence in the Middle East amid reported talks 25/03/2026 Middle East US sends 15-point peace plan to Iran while deploying troops in the region 25/03/2026 Middle East 'The humanitarian crisis here is worsening by the minute': Israel continues to bomb Lebanon 25/03/2026 Middle East US to deploy elite army brigade to Middle East: reports 24/03/2026 Middle East Pakistan’s prime minister says his nation is ready to facilitate talks to end Iran war 24/03/2026 Middle East Saudi leader said to be pushing Trump to continue war in Iran, New York Times reports 24/03/2026 Middle East War on Iran: 'Fought on faulty assumptions, notion of externally delivered regime change delusional' 24/03/2026 Middle East"
